# Act One

= Anna hears something she shouldn't.

INT. KITCHEN - DAY

A small kitchen, mid-afternoon light. ANNA (30s, careful) is making tea.
The kettle clicks off. She doesn't reach for it.

A faint, rhythmic *tap* comes from inside the pantry. She freezes.

ANNA
(under her breath)
Not again.

She sets the mug down. The tap stops. A long beat. Then it starts again,
slower this time, almost *deliberate*.

BEN (O.S.)
Anna? You okay in there?

ANNA
(too quickly)
Fine.

She walks to the pantry, hand hovering near the handle.

[[stage note: this is the longest single take in the scene — keep it slow]]

.HER POV - THE PANTRY DOOR

It is, somehow, slightly **ajar**.

CUT TO:

INT. KITCHEN - CONTINUOUS

She pulls the door open. Nothing. Just shelves of jars and a single,
half-empty bag of flour that has split down one seam, leaking a thin
white line onto the floor that leads, impossibly, toward the back wall.

ANNA
What.

She kneels, follows the line with her finger. It ends at a knot in the
floorboard she has never noticed before.

ANNA (CONT'D)
That's not.

She presses it. Nothing happens. She presses harder. The board sinks
half an inch and stops.

BEN (O.S.)
You sure you're okay?

= She decides not to answer.

ANNA
Hello?

BEN ^
(from the hall)
Did you say something?

INT. HALLWAY - CONTINUOUS

BEN (40s, kind, slightly out of focus on everything) stands at the foot
of the stairs holding a coffee mug, listening.

He waits. Nothing.

BEN
(to himself)
She's fine.

He climbs the stairs.

= Anna is not fine.

CUT TO:

INT. KITCHEN - CONTINUOUS

The pantry door is closed again. The flour line is gone. Anna stands
exactly where she was, mug in hand, as if she had never moved.

She looks at the kettle. The kettle is on.

ANNA
(quietly)
I didn't turn that back on.

# Act Two

= Anna goes looking for whatever is looking for her.

INT. CELLAR STAIRS - LATER

Anna descends, phone-torch on, free hand on the wall. The light catches
something faint scratched into the plaster — letters, almost worn out.

ANNA
"Don't open the…"

The bulb at the bottom of the stairs *pops*. Darkness, except the phone.

> THE END <
